Quantum Mechanics — David Tong (@mat-tong-quantum: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mat-sources) { r_0GY6BHCRA9CR5YGBY1AT9DRZY0
David Tong, University of Cambridge. [Author's course](https://davidtong.org/teaching/quantum-mechanics/), [complete 133-page notes](https://davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/quantum-mechanics/qm.pdf), with an accessible HTML alternative from the course page.

Read chapters 1–3 completely, working normalization, well, oscillator, tunnelling and operator calculations. Continue through chapter 4's angular momentum and atomic states for the magnetic and optical investigations. The final two-dimensional renormalisation discussion is a deeper continuation rather than an assumed shortcut to materials prediction.

The contents and selected wavefunction, inner-product and operator passages were inspected on 30 October 2026. These are the author's freely available lecture notes; the expanded commercial textbook is a separate work. No general open adaptation licence was established. Keep the notes and figures external and attribute the author.

**Return:** [Materials-engineering sources — reading and primary evidence](../Sources.lingua#r_51JAH6DB4WV2HZAB69G21ZHSMK).
